8 When something goes wrong
***************************

Start with ‘C-c r ?’.  It finds most problems and says what to do.

   • *A book doesn't open at my place.*  Is ‘readq-mode’ on?  Did the
     file move?  Then press ‘l’ on it in the dashboard to point readq to
     the new place.
   • *SumatraPDF doesn't save my page.*  readq learns it when you close
     the document in SumatraPDF.  Keep its option _Remember opened
     files_ on.
   • *mpv doesn't start.*  Check that ‘mpv’ runs in a terminal, or set
     ‘readq-mpv-program’.  For YouTube, update yt-dlp.
   • *Anki export fails.*  Open Anki first, with AnkiConnect installed.
   • *A figure shows as a link.*  Press ‘C-c C-x C-v’ in the note to
     show images.
   • *readq says the queue file changed and was not saved.*  Another
     Emacs, or a sync program, wrote it.  See *note Your data: Your
     data.
   • *Too much is due.*  Lower the priority of what matters less, pause
     books you are not reading now (‘x’), or lower
     ‘readq-daily-minutes’: readq spreads the rest.

   The full list of changes is in CHANGELOG.md
(https://github.com/n0w1ht/readq/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).  Problems and
ideas go to the issue tracker (https://github.com/n0w1ht/readq/issues).


